id: pm-slack-tfrk
title: Stabilise the changelog gate release date by deriving it from the calendar version instead of the clock
description: ""
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-24T09:22:20.539Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-24T09:36:28.066Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-24T09:23:43.683Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-24T09:23:43.683Z"
claim_principal: pi-agent
author: pi-agent
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-24T09:36:28.066Z","harness:claude-code","Completed the site coverage. The first pass flagged only the package.json scripts named changelog, leaving the three invocations in the release workflow unflagged. During a release the workflow generates the changelog and CI then checks it, so with the flag on only one side an untagged version whose calendar date is not today derives the heading from the clock on one side and from the version on the other, and the release fails on that divergence instead of on the stale date the flag exists to remove. Enumerated by grepping every tracked file for release-version-from-package rather than by reading the scripts that looked relevant. Seven sites in this package, four in package.json and three in release.yml, recount now four of four and three of three. Gates: changelog full then check reports up to date, pinned pm health --strict-exit exit 0."
notes[1]:
  - created_at: "2026-08-24T09:22:57.158Z"
    author: pi-agent
    text: "[{\"body\":\"Proof at version 2026.8.20 (untagged, not today): WITHOUT the date-from-version flag the generated heading is 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-24 (current UTC clock, flips at midnight); WITH the flag it is 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-20 (derived from the calendar version). Both runs used identical arguments plus --include-empty so the pending release section renders.\"}]"
    format: json
    data[1]{body}:
      "Proof at version 2026.8.20 (untagged, not today): WITHOUT the date-from-version flag the generated heading is 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-24 (current UTC clock, flips at midnight); WITH the flag it is 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-20 (derived from the calendar version). Both runs used identical arguments plus --include-empty so the pending release section renders."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  package.json,project,insert the date-from-version flag into the three changelog scripts and bump pm-changelog to ^2026.8.17
  package-lock.json,project,lockfile moved to pm-changelog 2026.8.17 which introduces the date-from-version flag
tests[4]{command,scope,note}:
  "npm run changelog:check",project,changelog gate stays green
  npm test,project,full unit test suite
  npm run coverage,project,coverage gate
  ./node_modules/.bin/pm health --strict-exit,project,pinned binary health check
close_reason: "Changelog scripts now pass the date-from-version flag (pm-changelog ^2026.8.17) so the no-tag release date derives from the calendar version instead of the UTC clock. Proof at version 2026.8.20: without-flag heading 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-24 vs with-flag heading 2026.8.20 - 2026-08-20. Verified: changelog:check green, npm test 80/80, coverage gate met, pm health --strict-exit exit 0."
body: ""
